# Crosskey sandbox (S-Pankki, Aktia, POP Pankki, Ålandsbanken, Morrow Bank, Resurs Bank).
#
#   cp banks/crosskey/sandbox.env.example banks/crosskey/sandbox.env   # never committed
#   # fill in the values, then:
#   set -a; . banks/crosskey/sandbox.env; set +a
#   go run ./cmd/obdev connect
#
# Portal: https://crosskey.io (sign up with an e-mail address)
#   1. Teams -> create a team -> Sandbox certificates -> generate. Save the TLS client
#      certificate, the digital signature certificate and both private keys to
#      banks/crosskey/cert/ (ignored by git).
#   2. Applications -> register an application for the team, with the redirect URL below.
#      It shows the Client ID and the X-API-Key.
#   3. Subscribe the application to the sandbox APIs of each bank (Account and Transaction,
#      Payment Initiation, Redirect Authorization). The application page then lists each
#      bank's sandbox test users.
# Guide: docs/crosskey.md

OBSDK_BANK=spankki          # spankki, aktia, poppankki, alandsbanken, morrowbank, resursbank
OBSDK_COUNTRY=FI            # alandsbanken: FI or SE; morrowbank: FI, NO, SE; resursbank: DK, FI, NO, SE
OBSDK_ENV=sandbox
# OBSDK_SEGMENT=business    # spankki, aktia

OBSDK_TLS_CERT=banks/crosskey/cert/tls.pem
OBSDK_TLS_KEY=banks/crosskey/cert/tls.key
OBSDK_SEAL_KEY=banks/crosskey/cert/signature.key
OBSDK_SEAL_CERT=banks/crosskey/cert/signature.pem
# Leave empty: the kid is the signature certificate's serial number (decimal), read from the certificate.
OBSDK_SEAL_KID=

OBSDK_CLIENT_ID=
OBSDK_REDIRECT_URL=https://example.com
# api_key = the application's X-API-Key.
OBSDK_EXTRA=api_key=

OBSDK_SESSION_FILE=banks/crosskey/sandbox.session.json
OBSDK_PSU_IP=203.0.113.7
OBSDK_PSU_USER_AGENT=obdev/0.1

# Sandbox test users (typed on the bank's login page, not read by any code): see the
# application's Sandboxes page. S-Pankki: customera / customerb, password 12345678.
# The callback (https://example.com/#code=...) must reach obdev within about 30 seconds.
